hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1101","On the authority of Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam, on the authority of Mulazim ibn Amr, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Badr, on the authority of Qais ibn Talq, who said: My father visited us one day in Ramadan, so he spent the evening with us and broke his fast, and he stayed with us that night and performed Witr prayers with us, then he went down to his mosque and prayed with his companions until he remained Then he brought a man from his companions and said: Perform the Witr prayer with your companions, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Do not perform the Witr prayer.” \"Night\""
